      challenge:
        "Create a release checklist and run your core flow on one physical device: pre-flight the whole submission (config, secrets, permissions with purpose strings, privacy declarations, assets, listings), run the device matrix — cold install, permission deny then grant, offline mid-task, relaunch, upgrade over real data — smoke-test the actual signed binary, submit with staged rollout, and monitor crash-free sessions for 48 hours. Then write the checklist down as a document with checkboxes, add every surprise the run produced as a new permanent line, and rehearse the rollback once — because the deliverable that outlasts this release is the process that makes the next one boring.",
